WEBVTT

00:00:00.970 --> 00:00:02.890
Oh, crap!

00:00:05.510 --> 00:00:07.860
Riko, you realize what time it is?

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:09.580
I know!

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:10.280
Ouch!

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:13.110
She's like this every morning.

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:18.330
I thought she'd become more of 
a lady after entering Fuji Girls'.

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:21.310
Give up already, Mom.

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:23.960
She's past the age of being 
what you want her to be.

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:26.670
I already think of her as my older brother.

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:29.250
Ren, you bastard!

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:31.610
Damn it, you violent woman!

00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:33.760
You know, this is why boys 
are always turning you down!

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:36.120
You brat!

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:39.040
If you're that bitter, why don't you 
get someone to confess to you?

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:40.560
It's happened to me.

00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:41.770
Huh?!

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:44.350
Enough! You're both going to be late!

00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:48.260
Rentaro, stop opening your sister's 
old wounds and get ready!

00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:49.600
Okay.

00:00:52.310 --> 00:00:54.110
<i>Another one just opened.</i>

00:00:54.590 --> 00:00:56.210
Riko, you can do it.

00:00:56.210 --> 00:00:57.570
<i>And again...</i>

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:01.910
I-I know you're made of the 
right stuff, Riko! Right? Right?

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:03.290
Oh, yeah.

00:01:03.290 --> 00:01:06.720
Remember our old neighbor, Satoshi-kun?

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:08.580
I ran into him the other day.

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:12.880
He used to look like a little girl,
 but he's grown quite manly.

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:16.340
According to his mother, 
he's very popular now.

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:21.020
I think it'd be good for you 
to act a little girlier, too.

00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:29.810
<i>I'll never... I'll never be...</i>

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:35.980
<i>Boys don't treat me like a girl.</i>

00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:38.200
<i>I never get past friendship, 
and I always get shot down.</i>

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:43.450
<i>I'll never be popular!</i>

00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:51.040
<i>Kurahashi Riko-san is wonderfully wild as always!</i>

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:23.000
<b>After School</b>

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:27.960
<b>The Terrible Legend of Riko</b>

00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:35.060
Riko, is something wrong?

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:38.280
Don't worry about it.

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:45.500
Come on, let's get to it.

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:46.780
Okay.

00:03:48.310 --> 00:03:53.180
<i>If I were as pretty and girly as 
Maki, I'm sure I'd be popular.</i>

00:03:53.570 --> 00:03:55.140
This time...

00:03:55.640 --> 00:03:59.760
We'll practice creating auras that'll make 
boys want to talk to us on the street!

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:03.340
<i>She's an idiot on the inside, though.</i>

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:06.220
Are you saying you want to be hit on?

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:08.590
What? N-No!

00:04:08.590 --> 00:04:10.470
Nothing that direct.

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:13.820
Just a casual greeting and a conversation...

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:16.940
As the first step, you know...

00:04:17.270 --> 00:04:19.100
Let's begin as friends!

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:20.850
Love and peace for all of humankind!

00:04:20.850 --> 00:04:22.560
The freedom heart is a world treasure!

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:23.930
I have a Guinness-level heart!

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:25.610
How are those related?

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:28.860
People often keep their distance from me.

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:30.630
You know I don't have many friends.

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:33.870
I thought boys might treat me the same way.

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:36.880
<i>She does seem too perfect on the outside.</i>

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:42.300
What if I secretly watch boys from 
the shadows, quivering in loneliness?

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:45.800
They might talk to you... 
to ask if you're all right.

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:48.340
You're lucky you have so many friends.

00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:51.770
You must know all the tricks 
to drawing others toward you.

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:53.500
You're a true master of love!

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:54.840
A popular girl!

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:58.690
<i>This lie really stings today.</i>

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:04.150
Anyway, the others sure are late.

00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:06.360
Suzu is out with a cold.

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:09.850
Something came up, so Eno's going home.

00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:11.080
I'm skipping, too.

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:13.080
Oh, I see.

00:05:13.270 --> 00:05:16.000
<i>I just can't stand this girl.</i>

00:05:19.430 --> 00:05:22.900
Shame I don't get to practice 
romance with the master.

00:05:24.810 --> 00:05:26.630
<i>Especially this side of her.</i>

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:29.960
What should we do, Riko?

00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:32.350
Ah, enough of this!

00:05:32.980 --> 00:05:35.700
Why don't we take the day 
off and have some fun?

00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:37.980
Didn't you say you wanted 
some hair accessories?

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:40.200
Oh! Yes, let's go!

00:05:47.450 --> 00:05:48.870
We bought some cute ones.

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:49.790
Yes.

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:52.530
Is it all right if we stop by the bookstore?

00:05:52.670 --> 00:05:53.580
Sure!

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:56.680
<i>This has been a nice change of pace.</i>

00:06:03.700 --> 00:06:04.420
Huh?

00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:07.880
<i>What is she doing here?</i>

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:11.450
Did you come to put your 
romantic efforts into practice?

00:06:11.450 --> 00:06:12.100
What?!

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:13.570
Good luck.

00:06:13.570 --> 00:06:14.390
I'll be watching.

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:18.270
D-Did we come here so boys would talk to us?

00:06:18.680 --> 00:06:19.650
<i>Hey!</i>

00:06:19.850 --> 00:06:22.040
Riko, show me how to do it.

00:06:22.040 --> 00:06:23.820
You heard her, Kurahashi.

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:26.780
Kurahashi?

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:28.720
<i>Wh-What am I going to do?</i>

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:30.600
<i>I wonder if anyone will talk to me...</i>

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:31.740
Riko?

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:38.190
<i>Someone's talking to me, but...</i>

00:06:38.620 --> 00:06:39.500
<i>Who?</i>

00:06:40.650 --> 00:06:41.950
It's really you, Riko!

00:06:41.950 --> 00:06:43.380
It's been so long.

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:44.350
Huh?

00:06:44.350 --> 00:06:47.300
I heard you'd gone to 
Fuji Girls'. I see it was true!

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:48.430
<i>Who?</i>

00:06:48.430 --> 00:06:50.230
<i>Who is this?</i>

00:06:50.230 --> 00:06:51.550
<i>I want to ask him.</i>

00:06:56.730 --> 00:06:58.510
Good to see you again!

00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:01.190
<i>I'm such an idiot.</i>

00:07:01.190 --> 00:07:02.370
An ex-boyfriend?

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:03.560
No!

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:06.690
Oh, someone you rejected?

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:08.640
No, he's...

00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:12.080
No, actually... that...

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:12.820
Huh?

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:16.010
That was a long time ago.

00:07:16.010 --> 00:07:17.740
I-It's...

00:07:18.100 --> 00:07:19.500
Damn it!

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:19.500
Hey, wait!

00:07:20.650 --> 00:07:22.120
Riko, you heartbreaker!

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:23.100
What?

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:24.510
I didn't think it was true.

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:25.760
I'm surprised.

00:07:26.560 --> 00:07:28.630
No, it's...

00:07:29.510 --> 00:07:30.610
Well, yeah.

00:07:30.610 --> 00:07:32.310
It happens a lot.

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:38.340
<i>I want to ask, I want to ask!</i>

00:07:38.340 --> 00:07:40.430
<i>I want to ask who he is!</i>

00:07:42.740 --> 00:07:45.400
<i>I don't remember him at all.</i>

00:07:45.660 --> 00:07:50.110
<i>He must be someone who used to like me...</i>

00:07:53.030 --> 00:07:54.160
Nee-chan?!

00:07:55.190 --> 00:07:56.700
Mom, it's an emergency!

00:07:56.700 --> 00:07:59.240
Nee-chan suddenly burst into 
flames on the side of the road!

00:07:59.240 --> 00:08:00.960
What's going on?!

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:04.070
<b>The Next Morning</b>

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:04.080
Ren-kun, do you want to 
go to school together?

00:08:04.260 --> 00:08:05.760
I'll go by myself.

00:08:06.050 --> 00:08:07.290
Aww...

00:08:07.630 --> 00:08:09.630
You should've gone with them.

00:08:09.630 --> 00:08:11.220
No way. It's too much hassle.

00:08:11.780 --> 00:08:14.790
At times like this, I'm jealous of Nee-chan.

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:24.140
Huh?

00:08:24.850 --> 00:08:26.940
You little brat.

00:08:32.550 --> 00:08:34.740
Riko, you heartbreaker.

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:36.990
Stop that.

00:08:37.460 --> 00:08:39.450
<i>I love that it's not a lie!</i>

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:42.360
How did you meet him?

00:08:42.360 --> 00:08:43.780
Was he a classmate?

00:08:43.780 --> 00:08:47.020
Sorry, but I don't remember.

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:49.210
You little devil!

00:08:49.210 --> 00:08:52.090
<i>I love that it's technically not a lie!</i>

00:08:52.380 --> 00:08:54.190
He called you by your first name,

00:08:54.190 --> 00:08:56.360
so I thought you must have 
had a special relationship.

00:08:56.610 --> 00:08:58.390
<i>Yeah, that's true.</i>

00:08:58.390 --> 00:09:02.100
<i>The only ones who call me Riko 
are cousins and childhood friends.</i>

00:09:02.470 --> 00:09:04.170
I admire that, though.

00:09:04.170 --> 00:09:06.890
I hope someone will call me Natsuo someday.

00:09:07.610 --> 00:09:12.190
I've already purchased an IC recorder 
to capture that shining moment!

00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:13.710
Go return that!

00:09:13.710 --> 00:09:16.240
See if they'll exchange 
what's inside your head, too!

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:20.140
You must have been special to him, though.

00:09:20.140 --> 00:09:22.490
Please try to remember, for his sake.

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:24.960
Okay.

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:32.170
<i>Who was that?</i>

00:09:32.680 --> 00:09:34.260
<i>I rejected him?</i>

00:09:34.260 --> 00:09:35.750
<i>A long time ago?</i>

00:09:36.140 --> 00:09:38.640
<i>I don't remember anything,</i>

00:09:39.210 --> 00:09:40.180
<i>but...</i>

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:42.310
By the way, Riko.

00:09:43.190 --> 00:09:45.310
What's going on with you and Ikezawa-kun?

00:09:45.630 --> 00:09:46.560
Who's that?

00:09:46.780 --> 00:09:48.560
You heartbreaker.

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:51.020
You could at least remember him.

00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:51.020
Ow!

00:09:51.880 --> 00:09:53.280
That hurt! What are you...

00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:57.870
I'm attending the cram school you went 
to for your entrance exams, remember?

00:09:57.870 --> 00:10:00.000
He stopped me to talk the other day.

00:10:00.250 --> 00:10:03.100
He asked me all about you.

00:10:03.100 --> 00:10:06.290
He was surprised when I told him 
you were on the student council.

00:10:06.700 --> 00:10:07.750
<i>Could it be?</i>

00:10:08.070 --> 00:10:09.330
When's your next lesson?

00:10:09.530 --> 00:10:11.290
Huh? It's today.

00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:12.590
I'll go with you.

00:10:21.340 --> 00:10:23.510
You seem strangely geared up.

00:10:23.510 --> 00:10:25.200
Y-You're just imagining things.

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:27.020
Oh, there's Ikezawa-kun.

00:10:27.020 --> 00:10:27.680
What?

00:10:30.020 --> 00:10:30.960
Which one?

00:10:30.960 --> 00:10:31.940
Right there.

00:10:32.180 --> 00:10:33.400
With the glasses.

00:10:33.720 --> 00:10:34.620
It's Yan!

00:10:34.620 --> 00:10:35.440
Yan?

00:10:36.600 --> 00:10:37.530
Kurahashi?

00:10:37.770 --> 00:10:39.870
Hey, Yan. It's been a while!

00:10:39.870 --> 00:10:41.240
Don't call me Yan.

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:43.910
That weird nickname has 
stuck to me, thanks to you.

00:10:44.470 --> 00:10:47.060
My name's Ikezawa Masaomi.

00:10:47.180 --> 00:10:48.870
You're totally ignoring my actual name.

00:10:48.870 --> 00:10:50.370
That's not true.

00:10:51.010 --> 00:10:51.650
See?

00:10:51.650 --> 00:10:55.370
<b>Ikezawa-kun</b>

00:10:52.270 --> 00:10:55.370
<b>Ikezawa</b>

00:10:52.900 --> 00:10:55.370
<b>Ikeyan</b>

00:10:53.520 --> 00:10:55.370
<b>Yanta</b>

00:10:54.150 --> 00:10:55.370
<b>Yan</b>

00:10:55.630 --> 00:10:58.130
What kind of free-form alteration is that?!

00:10:58.130 --> 00:10:59.850
I'm going now.

00:11:01.100 --> 00:11:03.650
I can't believe you're on the student council.

00:11:03.650 --> 00:11:05.720
Fuji Girls' has fallen far.

00:11:05.720 --> 00:11:06.900
What did you say?

00:11:06.900 --> 00:11:08.890
You haven't changed at all.

00:11:10.100 --> 00:11:11.920
<i>Guess it wasn't him.</i>

00:11:12.120 --> 00:11:13.650
<i>Of course it wasn't.</i>

00:11:13.650 --> 00:11:15.580
<i>There's no way I'd meet him so...</i>

00:11:15.580 --> 00:11:16.150
Yan!

00:11:16.400 --> 00:11:17.420
Don't call me Yan.

00:11:17.420 --> 00:11:19.270
Sorry I'm late.

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:25.490
Wait!

00:11:25.790 --> 00:11:27.120
Hey!

00:11:30.580 --> 00:11:32.710
<i>Who</i> hasn't changed?

00:11:41.960 --> 00:11:44.750
Hey, wait! Wait up!

00:11:45.990 --> 00:11:48.600
You, the one who confessed 
to me a long time ago!

00:11:49.060 --> 00:11:51.970
The one I rejected!

00:11:54.190 --> 00:11:56.110
D-Damn you!

00:11:59.690 --> 00:12:02.930
First you made fun of me with 
your friends, and now this?

00:12:03.170 --> 00:12:04.910
You're terrible.

00:12:04.910 --> 00:12:06.590
Y-You've got the wrong idea!

00:12:06.590 --> 00:12:07.660
How do you figure?

00:12:07.980 --> 00:12:09.870
Because I don't even remember.

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:14.440
I don't remember your confession, 
or turning you down at all!

00:12:14.440 --> 00:12:17.000
So I can't make fun of you for it!

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:18.380
That's even worse!

00:12:20.590 --> 00:12:22.300
You really don't remember?

00:12:24.220 --> 00:12:25.260
Sorry.

00:12:26.500 --> 00:12:30.280
Um, g-give me a hint?

00:12:31.720 --> 00:12:33.170
I had the wrong person.

00:12:33.170 --> 00:12:34.270
What? Hey, wait!

00:12:34.270 --> 00:12:35.730
Shut up, let go!

00:12:35.730 --> 00:12:37.470
But now I'm curious.

00:12:37.470 --> 00:12:40.650
It doesn't matter if you 
don't remember, stupid Riko.

00:12:48.920 --> 00:12:51.080
I don't care if your curiosity 
keeps you up at night!

00:12:51.240 --> 00:12:53.330
In fact, I hope it does!

00:12:55.560 --> 00:12:57.090
<i>Was that...</i>

00:13:02.740 --> 00:13:07.710
<i>For a second, I felt like 
I was about to remember...</i>

00:13:07.710 --> 00:13:09.760
Hey, Riko. Riko!

00:13:09.990 --> 00:13:11.570
What do you want?

00:13:11.570 --> 00:13:13.290
I had her send me a picture.

00:13:13.290 --> 00:13:14.500
Remember?

00:13:14.500 --> 00:13:16.580
I told you I ran into him the other day.

00:13:17.760 --> 00:13:18.610
Satoshi-kun.

00:13:23.030 --> 00:13:24.570
<b>Summer Vacation</b>

00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:25.700
<b>Children's Festival</b>

00:13:25.700 --> 00:13:29.280
I wanted to show you, so I had 
his mother take a picture.

00:13:29.280 --> 00:13:32.040
Satoshi-kun really has changed, hasn't he?

00:13:32.820 --> 00:13:38.260
When he was on your soccer 
team, he was so cute.

00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:40.550
<i>This is a trick!</i>

00:13:40.550 --> 00:13:43.040
<i>Of course I won't recognize 
him if he changed that much!</i>

00:13:43.190 --> 00:13:47.310
<i>Besides, I haven't seen him since 
he transferred away in third grade.</i>

00:13:47.790 --> 00:13:49.510
<i>It's no wonder I forgot.</i>

00:13:49.700 --> 00:13:52.180
Teammates are so nice, aren't they?

00:13:52.180 --> 00:13:54.140
When I asked if he remembered you,

00:13:54.140 --> 00:13:57.060
he said there was no way he would 
forget a friend he played with.

00:13:59.280 --> 00:14:00.260
Oh?

00:14:00.590 --> 00:14:03.110
If you lie down there, I'll step on you.

00:14:03.260 --> 00:14:04.570
Please do.

00:14:05.110 --> 00:14:06.780
No, that's gross.

00:14:08.040 --> 00:14:09.610
He used to live nearby.

00:14:09.880 --> 00:14:12.690
He was your teammate and childhood friend.

00:14:13.600 --> 00:14:14.490
And you...

00:14:14.490 --> 00:14:16.340
I know. Don't say it.

00:14:16.340 --> 00:14:19.300
I don't remember him confessing 
his feelings to me at all, either.

00:14:19.790 --> 00:14:21.830
He seems to be attending that cram school,

00:14:21.830 --> 00:14:23.420
so I'm going to go apologize to him.

00:14:26.080 --> 00:14:29.050
Would it be all right if I went with you?

00:14:29.050 --> 00:14:29.970
What?

00:14:30.260 --> 00:14:32.640
My grades have fallen lately.

00:14:32.640 --> 00:14:34.560
I'd been looking for a good cram school.

00:14:34.560 --> 00:14:36.270
You liar, you're at the top of your class.

00:14:36.480 --> 00:14:39.830
But I want to interact with boys, too!

00:14:39.830 --> 00:14:42.340
Our test run the other day was cut short!

00:14:42.340 --> 00:14:43.190
That was...

00:14:43.190 --> 00:14:46.040
I won't get in your way. Please!

00:14:46.040 --> 00:14:46.960
But...

00:14:46.960 --> 00:14:49.360
I've already looked up the school's address.

00:14:49.520 --> 00:14:50.900
I've acquired a schedule, too.

00:14:50.900 --> 00:14:52.420
Are you threatening me?

00:14:52.800 --> 00:14:56.570
<b>Irikimi 
Cram 
School</b>

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:56.020
Hey.

00:14:56.830 --> 00:14:58.980
Did something happen 
between you and Kurahashi?

00:14:59.710 --> 00:15:00.780
Not really.

00:15:00.780 --> 00:15:01.860
Nothing happened.

00:15:01.860 --> 00:15:03.380
You sprinted away from her.

00:15:03.580 --> 00:15:06.590
That's because I suddenly 
had to go to the bathroom.

00:15:06.790 --> 00:15:09.660
Seeing girls like her always 
makes my stomach hurt.

00:15:09.660 --> 00:15:10.560
Really?

00:15:10.900 --> 00:15:12.650
Today will be another tough day for you, then.

00:15:14.040 --> 00:15:15.140
Try not to wet yourself.

00:15:16.160 --> 00:15:18.020
Hey, I want to talk to you!

00:15:20.010 --> 00:15:22.100
Yan, talk to Maki.

00:15:22.370 --> 00:15:23.190
What?

00:15:23.190 --> 00:15:24.340
Thanks!

00:15:27.330 --> 00:15:29.360
Hey, hear me out!

00:15:32.980 --> 00:15:35.020
I-I'm sorry.

00:15:35.210 --> 00:15:37.280
I remembered afterwards.

00:15:37.280 --> 00:15:38.330
Oh, really?

00:15:38.330 --> 00:15:39.370
It doesn't matter.

00:15:39.750 --> 00:15:40.830
I'm going now.

00:15:41.380 --> 00:15:44.080
Um, I'm sorry, really!

00:15:44.080 --> 00:15:46.170
You've gotten so masculine, I didn't notice...

00:15:47.070 --> 00:15:48.920
It's not much of an excuse.

00:15:52.930 --> 00:15:55.390
I-I've gotten so... what?

00:15:55.680 --> 00:15:56.810
<i>Huh?</i>

00:15:56.990 --> 00:15:58.280
Th-That's right!

00:15:58.280 --> 00:16:00.480
You're so manly, I didn't recognize you!

00:16:00.760 --> 00:16:03.100
Unlike before, you're really hot now!

00:16:03.100 --> 00:16:05.440
You're a man from every angle!

00:16:05.440 --> 00:16:08.210
I... I guess you couldn't help it, then.

00:16:08.210 --> 00:16:09.260
<i>All right!</i>

00:16:09.600 --> 00:16:11.130
Anyway, um...

00:16:12.520 --> 00:16:14.250
when did you confess to me?

00:16:14.250 --> 00:16:18.840
Your personality hasn't 
changed at all, though.

00:16:19.200 --> 00:16:21.510
But, you're on the student council, right?

00:16:21.510 --> 00:16:22.620
Yan told me.

00:16:23.160 --> 00:16:24.780
I can't even imagine it.

00:16:26.130 --> 00:16:28.250
You still look the same when you laugh!

00:16:28.250 --> 00:16:29.500
So cute!

00:16:31.110 --> 00:16:33.580
<b>Missed something 
important again</b>

00:16:36.650 --> 00:16:38.470
<i>Wh-What should I do?</i>

00:16:38.610 --> 00:16:40.500
<i>I should introduce myself first, right?</i>

00:16:41.070 --> 00:16:43.600
H-Hello, Yan-san.

00:16:43.900 --> 00:16:45.520
Yan-san? Um...

00:16:45.840 --> 00:16:47.110
<i>Who are you calling Yan?</i>

00:16:49.720 --> 00:16:50.740
Hello.

00:16:51.060 --> 00:16:53.320
It's a beautiful evening glow.

00:16:53.830 --> 00:16:55.950
What are you trying to do?

00:16:56.340 --> 00:16:58.580
You speak Japanese well.

00:16:58.580 --> 00:17:00.420
Well, I <i>am </i>Japanese.

00:17:00.420 --> 00:17:02.030
Are you making fun of me?

00:17:02.030 --> 00:17:03.330
No, I didn't mean...

00:17:03.630 --> 00:17:06.310
You didn't respond, so I thought 
you might be an exchange student.

00:17:06.310 --> 00:17:07.750
I'm obviously not.

00:17:08.100 --> 00:17:12.670
You think you can make fun of people 
just because you're kind of cute, don't you?

00:17:20.600 --> 00:17:22.320
Why are you reacting like that?

00:17:22.320 --> 00:17:23.620
That doesn't make sense!

00:17:23.620 --> 00:17:27.010
But... I-I've never had a boy

00:17:27.010 --> 00:17:30.940
call me c-cute before.

00:17:32.570 --> 00:17:33.490
What?

00:17:33.490 --> 00:17:35.420
Wh-What are you, some kind of idiot?!

00:17:35.420 --> 00:17:36.200
Huh?!

00:17:37.090 --> 00:17:38.220
<i>What is going on?</i>

00:17:38.220 --> 00:17:40.260
<i>He called me cute when he 
thought I made fun of him.</i>

00:17:40.260 --> 00:17:42.950
<i>Why is he calling me stupid now?</i>

00:17:42.950 --> 00:17:44.140
Are you a tsundere?!

00:17:44.140 --> 00:17:45.580
What are you talking about?!

00:17:46.370 --> 00:17:49.620
I don't understand boys!

00:17:49.620 --> 00:17:50.880
Hey!

00:17:51.470 --> 00:17:54.120
Th-That's what <i>I</i> want to say.

00:17:54.120 --> 00:17:55.480
I don't understand her at all.

00:17:56.860 --> 00:17:58.180
Riko!

00:17:58.180 --> 00:17:59.970
Sorry about that, Maki.

00:17:59.970 --> 00:18:01.120
Riko!

00:18:02.370 --> 00:18:05.390
Yan-san called me cute.

00:18:06.120 --> 00:18:07.810
<i>You're cute.</i>

00:18:07.810 --> 00:18:09.650
<i>R-Really?</i>

00:18:09.890 --> 00:18:11.060
Yan did?

00:18:11.060 --> 00:18:13.860
But then he called me 
stupid immediately after.

00:18:14.680 --> 00:18:17.010
<i>You took that seriously? Are you stupid?</i>

00:18:17.010 --> 00:18:17.610
<i>What?</i>

00:18:17.810 --> 00:18:19.440
Yan's terrible!

00:18:19.440 --> 00:18:21.120
I'm gonna have a little chat with him!

00:18:22.670 --> 00:18:24.350
Wh-What was that?

00:18:25.280 --> 00:18:27.370
Oh, Nagi. How'd it go with Kurahashi?

00:18:29.600 --> 00:18:31.000
I don't understand.

00:18:31.320 --> 00:18:33.340
I don't understand any of them.

00:18:33.340 --> 00:18:35.330
<b>The Next Day</b>

00:18:35.740 --> 00:18:37.090
What are you reading?

00:18:37.110 --> 00:18:43.590
<b>The Life of an Amorous Man</b>

00:18:37.330 --> 00:18:41.140
It seems not all men are gentlemen like Huggy.

00:18:41.140 --> 00:18:43.600
I'm reading to expand my knowledge.

00:18:47.060 --> 00:18:50.050
<b>Marquis
 de Sade</b>

00:18:47.700 --> 00:18:50.060
Don't choose books that'll 
create new misconceptions.

00:18:50.840 --> 00:18:52.320
Boys are so...

00:18:52.320 --> 00:18:55.580
If you put them on the same level 
as these, you'll only hurt yourself.

00:18:55.580 --> 00:18:57.860
I wasn't ready for an actual experience yet.

00:18:57.860 --> 00:18:59.640
I must practice more.

00:19:00.070 --> 00:19:01.400
I know!

00:19:01.400 --> 00:19:05.650
Today's subject will be techniques for 
meeting only boys who are your type.

00:19:05.650 --> 00:19:06.880
There are none.

00:19:08.370 --> 00:19:10.970
I'm jealous of the girl 
who asked us for advice.

00:19:11.280 --> 00:19:15.180
She's met someone she won't give 
up on, no matter how much it hurts.

00:19:15.180 --> 00:19:16.520
That girl, huh?

00:19:16.520 --> 00:19:19.150
I wish she'd tell us if anything 
happened after that.

00:19:20.290 --> 00:19:21.680
I-It's an emergency!

00:19:22.410 --> 00:19:23.010
What is it?

00:19:23.540 --> 00:19:25.980
We got another request for romantic 
advice in the suggestion box.

00:19:25.980 --> 00:19:26.640
What?

00:19:27.030 --> 00:19:28.720
"I just started going out with my boyfriend..."

00:19:28.720 --> 00:19:30.240
They're already moving forward!

00:19:30.240 --> 00:19:33.270
"What should I say if I just want to be friends?"

00:19:33.610 --> 00:19:35.020
What?

00:19:35.230 --> 00:19:36.900
How did it progress that far?

00:19:37.890 --> 00:19:38.960
It's an emergency!

00:19:38.960 --> 00:19:40.660
We've already got an 
emergency on our hands!

00:19:40.660 --> 00:19:43.240
We received another note in 
the suggestion box, and...

00:19:43.500 --> 00:19:45.870
What? Hold on.

00:19:45.870 --> 00:19:46.860
Look at this.

00:19:46.860 --> 00:19:49.160
It was in the suggestion box 
in the south building.

00:19:49.160 --> 00:19:51.160
<b>Romantic Advice

00:19:53.400 --> 00:19:55.380
This is the previous note.

00:19:55.640 --> 00:19:58.000
This is the one Suzu brought 
from the north building.

00:19:58.140 --> 00:20:00.590
This is the one Enomoto-senpai 
brought from the south building.

00:20:00.890 --> 00:20:03.750
Their handwriting and situations 
are completely different.

00:20:03.750 --> 00:20:06.640
The one who wants to 
break up isn't the first girl.

00:20:07.000 --> 00:20:09.430
Let's calm down and get 
a grasp of the situation.

00:20:09.430 --> 00:20:12.950
We'll split up and check 
the other suggestion boxes.

00:20:13.120 --> 00:20:14.310
Also...

00:20:17.320 --> 00:20:21.140
In order to respond to the request, 
we should simulate a breakup.

00:20:21.140 --> 00:20:22.320
Calm down.

00:20:23.090 --> 00:20:25.320
<b>What can I do to make 
a boy's heart skip and 
get his attention?</b>

00:20:23.340 --> 00:20:25.320
A third one from in front of the gym.

00:20:25.690 --> 00:20:27.620
A fourth from the club room's building.

00:20:29.450 --> 00:20:31.590
The other notes were normal.

00:20:31.590 --> 00:20:33.960
That's four requests total for romantic advice.

00:20:34.180 --> 00:20:38.880
The girls who attended the meeting 
when our lab was exposed...

00:20:38.880 --> 00:20:43.380
After that broadcast, they must think 
we're offering romantic advice anytime.

00:20:43.920 --> 00:20:46.930
If the rumor spreads, the 
teachers might find out.

00:20:47.400 --> 00:20:52.040
We haven't heard any rumors yet, 
so we should still be all right.

00:20:52.320 --> 00:20:56.030
Even if they do find out, we're 
keeping a close eye on our data.

00:20:56.030 --> 00:20:57.330
There's no evidence.

00:20:57.420 --> 00:20:59.480
I've been learning from someone.

00:21:00.740 --> 00:21:02.440
What should we do about these requests?

00:21:02.440 --> 00:21:05.360
We can't take over the broadcast room again.

00:21:05.570 --> 00:21:06.570
Can we ignore them?

00:21:06.780 --> 00:21:08.080
I'd rather not.

00:21:08.210 --> 00:21:10.970
Besides, if we only respond to one student,

00:21:10.970 --> 00:21:13.290
people might think we're playing 
favorites and lose faith in us.

00:21:15.260 --> 00:21:17.730
This has become a tough problem.

00:21:17.730 --> 00:21:19.150
You're right.

00:21:19.150 --> 00:21:20.250
It really has.

00:21:20.570 --> 00:21:23.040
So, what's the toughest problem?

00:21:23.040 --> 00:21:25.620
Conducting our romantic research, of course.

00:21:25.620 --> 00:21:27.680
And not having a means to convey our answers.

00:21:29.000 --> 00:21:33.480
So your romantic research has something 
to do with the suggestion boxes.

00:21:33.480 --> 00:21:34.320
What?

00:21:34.320 --> 00:21:35.770
Wh-Who is she?

00:21:35.770 --> 00:21:37.500
I knew you could do it, Momo-senpai!

00:21:37.500 --> 00:21:39.440
We've got valuable testimony now!

00:21:39.860 --> 00:21:41.490
This scoop will be...

00:21:41.490 --> 00:21:42.610
Nana-chan.

00:21:42.800 --> 00:21:45.820
Sorry for causing trouble.

00:21:46.090 --> 00:21:47.930
Come on, let's go.

00:21:52.200 --> 00:21:55.320
You shouldn't have said that, Nana-chan.

00:21:55.320 --> 00:21:57.030
I was so happy, I couldn't help it.

00:21:57.030 --> 00:21:59.380
After all, with that scoop...

00:21:59.440 --> 00:22:00.880
Last Boss

00:22:01.080 --> 00:22:04.720
We'll finally be able to outwit 
our old foe, Mizushima Sayori.

00:22:04.720 --> 00:22:06.550
Nana-chan, too loud.

00:22:07.170 --> 00:22:10.600
Wh-Who were they?

00:22:11.500 --> 00:22:13.040
I remember now.

00:22:13.920 --> 00:22:17.440
They're Minami-senpai and Ichikawa-san, 
from the newspaper association.

00:22:17.440 --> 00:22:18.690
The newspaper?

00:22:19.730 --> 00:22:21.690
This really is becoming...

00:22:21.690 --> 00:22:23.720
...a huge problem.

00:23:57.180 --> 00:24:02.860
<b>Preview</b>

00:23:58.330 --> 00:24:00.160
<i>You're terrible, Riko.</i>

00:24:00.160 --> 00:24:03.020
<i>I kind of agree, too.</i>

00:24:03.290 --> 00:24:05.680
<i>But Riko is popular.</i>

00:24:05.680 --> 00:24:09.400
<i>It's not her fault she can't remember 
every boy who has confessed his love for her.</i>

00:24:09.400 --> 00:24:10.740
<i>Y-Yeah, that's it.</i>

00:24:10.740 --> 00:24:11.800
<i>That's right!</i>

00:24:11.800 --> 00:24:12.680
<i>Yeah, that's right.</i>

00:24:12.680 --> 00:24:14.770
<i>I couldn't remember my boyfriend's name, either.</i>

00:24:14.770 --> 00:24:18.930
<i>I deleted all his emails, thinking they were
 spam, and eventually broke up with him.</i>

00:24:18.930 --> 00:24:20.930
<i>You're right, I'm terrible.</i>

00:24:21.120 --> 00:24:25.020
<i>I'm so sorry I forgot you!</i>

00:24:22.880 --> 00:24:27.010
<b>To the Kurahashi House!</b>

00:24:27.010 --> 00:24:30.020
<b>Don't miss the next episode!</b>
